      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT to understand the code before improving it.Now I understand the test. It verifies that `FilterListIterator.hasNext()` caches its look-ahead result — calling it twice on a single-element list should exhaust the underlying iterator on the first call, but still return `true` on the second call from the cached value.\n\nLet me write the improved version.Now I'll compile-check the file.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored test adds a descriptive Javadoc comment explaining the caching behavior under test, renames variables to meaningful names (`targetElement`, `singleElementList`, `underlyingIterator`, `matchesTarget`, `filterIterator`, `secondHasNextResult`), adds inline comments clarifying what each step does, and removes unused imports — all while preserving the exact same method calls, arguments, and assertions as the original."
